  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 808.26 Benzo(a)pyrene (PAHs)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 808.26 Benzo(a)pyrene (PAHs). For benzo(a)pyrene (PAH) violations, the statement shall read as follows:\n\n“Some people who drink water containing benzo(a)pyrene in excess of the MCL over many years may experience reproductive difficulties and may have an increased risk of getting cancer.”\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Dw 800) #9730, eff 6-30-10; ss by #12675, eff 1-1-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw800.html"
